@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-loads-under-node
`@pulls.review/core` MUST load under plain Node: no Settings, vue-i18n, `localStorage`,
`document` or Vite-only syntax inside it. Callers pass model settings and locale in
(architecture, Layout).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] engine-brief-is-openui-data
A brief or tour page is written in OpenUI Lang against the component library in
`brief.ts`; components take references (a changed path and line), never retyped data, and
an unknown component never renders. Only the Lang is stored; clients get a plain tree,
never the Lang, and output is data, never executed (architecture, The brief).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-tours-vary-their-form
The tour instructions ask the model to use the OpenUI components so each stop takes the
form that reads best (a flow, a table, a tree, code, a callout), not the same paragraphs
every time ("it looks a bit boring to read", recording 15 Oct 13:54, 07:46 to 08:14;
K17).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] engine-mentions-are-links
An analysis run for the app writes every place it names as a repository-relative
Markdown link (`MENTION_RULE`), which clients turn into a jump to that line (rule 96;
architecture, Sharing).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-shapes-are-schemas
Canonical shapes (`DiffsPayload`, `GroupedResult`, `PrCacheEntry`, ...) are valibot
schemas first, validated where data is untrusted or versioned: a provider's raw answer
and an entry read back from storage (architecture, Canonical data structures).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] engine-files-keyed-by-sha
Every `FileChange` carries a `sha` (GitHub's blob SHA, else one read from the patch's
`index` line, else a SHA-256 of the patch), and persisted review state is keyed by it
(architecture, Canonical data structures).
